   "isFreePreview": true,
   "description": "Khung môn học theo syllabus FLM chính thức.",
   "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">BFT201 · Section 0 · Lesson 0.6</span>\n<h2>Student tasks & constructive questions</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">The rules you are held to (attendance, preparation, exam eligibility) — verbatim.</p>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM · Syllabus ID 14413 · Decision 968/QĐ-ĐHFPT dated 07/08/2026 · collected 08/11/2026</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">BFT201 · Mục 0 · Bài 0.6</span>\n<h2>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên & câu hỏi kiến tạo</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">Những quy định bạn phải tuân theo (chuyên cần, chuẩn bị bài, điều kiện dự thi) — nguyên văn.</p>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: FLM · Syllabus ID 14413 · QĐ 968/QĐ-ĐHFPT ngày 07/08/2026 · thu ngày 08/11/2026</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Student tasks (verbatim)</h3>\n<p>- Students must attend more than 80% of contact slots in order to be accepted to the final examination.<br><br>- Student is responsible to do all exercises, workshops, assignments and case studies given by instructor in class or at home and submit on time<br><br>- Read the assigned textbook sections before each session; sections marked as background reading are self-study and are not assessed in depth<br><br>- Use laptop in class only for learning purpose<br><br>- Promptly access to the <a href=\"http://flm.fpt.edu.vn\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">http://flm.fpt.edu.vn</a> for up-to-date course information</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên (nguyên văn)</h3>\n<p>- Students must attend more than 80% of contact slots in order to be accepted to the final examination.<br><br>- Student is responsible to do all exercises, workshops, assignments and case studies given by instructor in class or at home and submit on time<br><br>- Read the assigned textbook sections before each session; sections marked as background reading are self-study and are not assessed in depth<br><br>- Use laptop in class only for learning purpose<br><br>- Promptly access to the <a href=\"http://flm.fpt.edu.vn\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">http://flm.fpt.edu.vn</a> for up-to-date course information</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Constructive questions (20)</h3>\n<p>Questions the syllabus asks you to think through before or during the session — try answering them yourself first.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Câu hỏi kiến tạo (20)</h3>\n<p>Câu hỏi syllabus yêu cầu bạn suy nghĩ trước/trong buổi học — tự trả lời trước khi xem bài.</p></div>\n<table>\n  <thead><tr><th>Session<br><small>Buổi</small></th><th>Code<br><small>Mã</small></th><th>Question (verbatim)<br><small>Câu hỏi (nguyên văn)</small></th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td>1</td><td>CQ1</td><td>Explain why a modern bank is a technology business, and compare an incumbent bank with a digital-first challenger on cost base, technology and customer proposition.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>5</td><td>CQ2</td><td>Map a modern banking product or service to the technology and payment infrastructure needed to deliver it.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>7</td><td>CQ3</td><td>Explain what a bank inherits from decades of banking technology, and why legacy systems make digital change slow, costly and risky.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>8</td><td>CQ4</td><td>Explain the roles of banks, challengers, payment schemes and processors in the current banking ecosystem.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>10</td><td>CQ5</td><td>Draw a simple model of a bank and explain what the core banking platform must do to open an account, hold balances and process transactions.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>12</td><td>CQ6</td><td>Explain what a banking database must guarantee for a transaction, and evaluate database architecture options for a banking system.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>13</td><td>CQ7</td><td>Explain how a bank stays available to its customers and recovers from failure, and assess an outage against those measures.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>15</td><td>CQ8</td><td>Explain why a single customer view is difficult to achieve in a bank, and what business problems its absence creates.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>17</td><td>CQ9</td><td>Explain why legacy transaction processing survives in banks and what constraints it places on a new digital proposition.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>19</td><td>CQ10</td><td>Design a secure authentication and digital onboarding journey that balances customer friction, fraud risk and identity requirements.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>21</td><td>CQ11</td><td>Evaluate what a banking or Open Banking API allows a third party to do, and what risks and controls it requires.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>23</td><td>CQ12</td><td>Explain how a bank turns transaction data into management and regulatory reporting, and where big data adds value.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>25</td><td>CQ13</td><td>Evaluate the role of branch and ATM technology in a digital-first bank, and decide what should be retained, automated or withdrawn.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>28</td><td>CQ14</td><td>Design a cross-channel customer journey that remains consistent, available, secure and accessible across mobile, web and assisted channels.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>32</td><td>CQ15</td><td>Trace a retail credit application through decisioning, and identify where automation adds most value and most risk.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>36</td><td>CQ16</td><td>Explain how a bank uses technology to verify customers, screen against sanctions lists and detect money laundering, and assess the customer-friction trade-off.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>38</td><td>CQ17</td><td>Trace a card payment from the terminal to the issuer, and explain the role, revenue and risk of each party in the four-party model.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>44</td><td>CQ18</td><td>Compare batch, instant and high-value payment schemes, and explain how a payment instruction is created, addressed, screened and reconciled.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>48</td><td>CQ19</td><td>Translate a regulatory requirement such as payment regulation, data protection or Open Banking into concrete technology and data obligations.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>57</td><td>CQ20</td><td>Develop and defend a digital banking technology solution that connects the business problem, solution architecture, channels, payments, risks and regulation.</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">Everything in the tables above is copied <strong>verbatim</strong> from the university's FLM page (in English, as published) so you can check it against the copy your lecturer gives you: <a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=14413\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=14413</a> (needs your FPT login). If FLM publishes a newer syllabus, FLM wins.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">Mọi thứ trong các bảng trên được chép <strong>nguyên văn</strong> từ trang FLM của trường (bằng tiếng Anh, đúng như trường công bố) để bạn đối chiếu với bản giảng viên phát: <a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=14413\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=14413</a> (cần đăng nhập tài khoản FPT). Nếu FLM công bố bản syllabus mới hơn thì theo FLM.</div></div>"
